      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MATTHEW GUARNIERI, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Intel Corporation Investment Policy Committee (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1113(2) of ERISA requires that claims for breach of fiduciary duty be brought within three years of when the plaintiff first had actual knowledge of the breach."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Intel Corporation Investment Policy Committee (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit was wrong to read the statute to require proof of subjective awareness."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Most people don't read them. MR. VERRILLI: You know, I -- I -- I JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Or many. Many people don't read them. So how do you have actual knowledge if you haven't read it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But, Mr. Verrilli, we do have the six-year outer limit, and then there's a special shorter limit if you have actual knowledge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. VERRILLI: There's no legal obligation to do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the plaintiff visited the website 68 times and clicked on 1,000 links"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What would the circumstantial evidence be?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Congress said that a plaintiff must have actual knowledge, it meant what we all understand that phrase to mean, that the plaintiff himself must have real awareness."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wessler",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WESSLER: Right. So there is this, I think, separate question that is not in front of the Court right now, which is, Justice Kagan, what you've identified, how much do you need to know that there's been a breach of ERISA. Now I think the Ninth Circuit articulated the correct standard in this case. But this Court is not being asked in this case to decide that question because, as -- again, as I said, as the Petitioners have framed this question, they've asked the Court to assume that all the relevant information was contained in the disclosures and that, had a participant read those disclosures, they would have the necessary knowledge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1116",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
